<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="AARCH64:LE:64:v8A:default">
<!--
    A Mach-O whose load commands name bytes past the end of the file.

    Issue: a truncated or hand-edited Mach-O - a partial download, a memory
    dump cut short, a carved file - failed the whole load with "Invalid Mach-O
    symbol table offset or size" (or "unreadable segment data"), although every
    byte of code that is present can be read.

    Stage / sub-stage: P1 container parse, the Mach-O range tolerance
    (`kuna-analysis/src/loader/kuna_machotolerance.rs
    (clamp_out_of_file_ranges)`), applied at `load file` beside the ELF and PE
    header repairs. Each segment, section, symbol table and string table that
    runs past the end of the file is clamped, in a copy of the image, to the
    bytes present.

    The XML wrapper only supplies the harness architecture. The fixture
    `macho_truncated_arm64` is the first 0x600 bytes of
    `macho_unwind_only_arm64`: __TEXT is cut short and __LINKEDIT, with the
    symbol and string tables, is gone.

    The image loads, `main` (from LC_MAIN) and the `__unwind_info` starts are
    listed, and `main` decompiles.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c0035fd6
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/macho_truncated_arm64</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>functions</com>
  <com>load function main</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="MACHOTRUNCATED #1: the truncated image loads and lists its entry" min="1" max="1">0x10000040c main</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="MACHOTRUNCATED #2: the unwind starts inside the bytes present are listed" min="1" max="1">0x1000003bc sub_1000003bc</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="MACHOTRUNCATED #3: the entry decompiles" min="1" max="1">main\(</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
